{"status":"ready","content":"The mean of {4, -19} is (4 + (-19))/2 = -15/2.\r\n\r\nDeviations from the mean:\r\n- 4 - (-15/2) = 4 + 15/2 = 23/2\r\n- -19 - (-15/2) = -19 + 15/2 = -23/2\r\n\r\nSum of squared deviations:\r\n(23/2)² + (-23/2)² = 529/4 + 529/4 = 529/2\r\n\r\nSample variance = (529/2)/(2-1) = 529/2\r\n\r\nSample standard deviation = √(529/2) = 23/√2 = 23√2/2\r\n\r\n$\\boxed{\\dfrac{23\\sqrt{2}}{2}}$\r\n","path":"responses/claude-sonnet-4-6/livebench-048-math.txt","size":365,"mtime":1779367863}